Below is the list of books I highly recommend for those also interested in the movers in AI:
1. The Nvidia Way by Tae Kim [this is about the history and culture of Nvidia, and the history of Jensen Huang]
2. The Thinking Machine by Stephen Witt [deeper dive into the personal story of Jensen]
3. Chip War by Chris Miller [excellent account of the history of today's key players in the AI hardware industry]
4. The Optimist by Keach Hagey [story of Sam Altman and co-founding of OpenAI]
